## 10. IFC-Specific Guidelines
### 10.1 Model Handling
- Process IFC models client-side only
- Implement proper cleanup of WebGL resources
- Support for IFC2x3 and IFC4 standards
- Extract and display IFC metadata

### 10.2 Performance Optimization
- Implement LOD (Level of Detail) for complex models
- Use spatial indexing for large scenes
- Implement visibility culling
- Profile and optimize render loops

### 10.3 Annotation System
- Store annotations in JSON format
- Link annotations to IFC elements by GUID
- Support for different annotation types
- Version annotations with timestamps

## 11. Development Log Protocol
### 11.1 Activation
- Log explicitly when requested (`"Devlog what we did"`).
- Do not store logs in memory.

### 11.2 Structure
- Location: `/dev-logs/`
- Format: Markdown
- Filename: `YYYYMMDD-dev-log.md`

### 11.3 Content of file
- Title: # Devlog for YYYY-MM-DD
- Time Markers: HH:MM - Entry description
- IFC Model Details (if applicable):
  - Model size and complexity
  - Processing time
  - Memory usage
- Changes Made:
  - File: `path/to/file`
  - Change: Description
  - Performance Impact: Notes on rendering/processing
  - Reason: Justification
- Issues and Solutions: 
  - Issue: Problem description
  - Solution: Implementation
  - IFC-Specific Considerations: Any model-related challenges
- Next Steps:
  - Pending tasks
  - Performance optimizations needed
  - Future IFC-related improvements
